orkloads\n\n---\n\n## When to use each\n\n**Default (usually mode 1 or 2):**\n- Most users don't need to change this\n- The driver handles context management automatically\n\n**Mode 4:**\n- Debugging CCS-related issues\n- Testing specific context scheduling behaviors\n- Advanced performance tuning for particular workloads\n\n---\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f **A note of caution:** I'm not fully certain about the exact semantics of each mode number, and these details can vary between driver versions. The Intel Xe driver documentation and kernel source are the authoritative sources.\n\nWould you like me to help you find the specific documentation or kernel source that describes these modes in detail? That would give you the precise, current definitions rather than relying on my potentially outdated knowledge."}